      "description": "This course introduces learners to the fundamentals of Agentic AI and modern AI agent systems. Learners will understand the difference between traditional AI, generative AI, and agentic AI, and explore how agents use reasoning, planning, tools, memory, and feedback to accomplish complex tasks. The course covers agent architectures, tool calling, workflows, autonomous decision-making, and multi-agent collaboration. Learners will also gain hands-on experience building simple AI agents using frameworks such as LangChain and LangGraph. By the end of the course, learners will be able to explain core agentic AI concepts, design basic agent workflows, integrate tools with agents, and identify suitable real-world enterprise use cases for agentic systems.",
