    {
      "id": "24",
      "sectionId": "10",
      "title": "ARTICLE TESTING",
      "contentType": "ARTICLE",
      "contentUrl": null,
      "description": "Here is some testing text for an Article content type in your LMS:\n\nTitle: Introduction to Agentic AI\n\nArticle Content:\n\nAgentic AI represents a new generation of artificial intelligence systems that can understand goals, reason about tasks, make decisions, use external tools, and take actions with limited human intervention.\n\nUnlike traditional AI systems that typically respond to a predefined request, AI agents can follow a multi-step process to accomplish a goal. An agent may analyze the user's request, create a plan, retrieve information, call an API or tool, evaluate the result, and decide what to do next.\n\nKey Components of Agentic AI\n\n1. Reasoning\nAgents analyze information and determine the appropriate next step based on the given goal.\n\n2. Planning\nAn agent can break a complex task into smaller, manageable steps and execute them in sequence.\n\n3. Tool Usage\nAgents can interact with external tools such as databases, APIs, search engines, calculators, and business applications.\n\n4. Memory\nMemory allows an agent to maintain relevant information from previous interactions and use it when making future decisions.\n\n5. Decision Making\nAgents evaluate available information and select an appropriate action to achieve their objectives.\n\nExample\n\nConsider an employee asking:\n\n\"Find my remaining leave balance and suggest suitable dates for a vacation.\"\n\nAn Agentic AI system could identify the employee, retrieve leave information from an HR system, check the company holiday calendar, analyze available dates, and provide suitable recommendations.\n\nAgentic AI vs Generative AI\n\nGenerative AI primarily focuses on generating content such as text, images, code, or summaries in response to prompts. Agentic AI goes a step further by using AI models as part of a larger system that can reason, plan, interact with tools, and perform actions.\n\nAgentic AI is therefore useful for applications such as customer support, enterprise automation, financial analysis, software development, research assistants, and workflow automation.\n\nKey Takeaway\n\nAgentic AI enables AI systems to move from simply answering questions to achieving goals through reasoning, planning, tool usage, and actions. Understanding these concepts is the foundation for building reliable and useful AI agents.",
      "duration": 10,
      "exactDurationSeconds": 0,
      "durationSource": "CALCULATED",
      "durationMetadata": null,
