 importance of every token relative to every other.\",\"Parallelizable\",\"Processes entire sequences simultaneously, unlike RNNs.\",\"Foundation Models\",\"GPT, BERT, and T5 all derive from this architecture.\"],\"color\":\"from-purple-500/20 to-pink-500/10 border-purple-500/30\"},{\"slideNum\":5,\"tag\":\"Slide 5\",\"heading\":\"Transfer Learning & Hugging Face\",\"subheading\":\"Instead of training from scratch, start from a pretrained model and fine-tune on your specific task — saving time, data, and compute.\",\"bullets\":[\"Pretrained Model\",\"Learned general features on massive data\",\"Task Model\",\"Ready for deployment with strong baseline\",\"Fine-Tune\",\"Adapt final layers to your dataset\",\"Why Transfer Learning?\",\"Less Data\",\"Faster Training\",\"Lower Compute\",\"Hugging Face Ecosystem\",\"Thousands of pretrained models across NLP, vision, and audio\",\"Unified tokenizers and dataset libraries\",\"Model Hub for sharing and versioning\",\"transformers\",\"and\",\"accelerate\",\"for fine-tuning\"],\"color\":\"from-red-500/20 to-rose-500/10 border-red-500/30\"},{\"slideNum\":6,\"tag\":\"Slide 6\",\"heading\":\"Distributed Training\",\"subheading\":\"Modern models are too large for a single GPU. Distributed strategies split the workload across devices to train faster and at greater scale.\",\"bullets\":[\"Data Parallelism\",\"Split batches across GPUs; each holds a full model copy.\",\"Model Parallelism\",\"Split model layers across GPUs for models that don&apos;t fit in memory.\",\"Pipeline Parallelism\",\"Divide the model into stages processed sequentially across devices.\",\"FSDP / ZeRO\",\"Shard optimizer states and gradients to dramatically reduce memory footprint.\"],\"color\":\"from-amber-500/20 to-yellow-500/10 border-amber-500/30\"},{\"slideNum\":7,\"tag\":\"Slide 7\",\"heading\":\"Model Registry\",\"subheading\":\"What is a Model Registry?\",\"bullets\":[\"A centralized system to\",\"store, version, and govern\",\"ML models throughout their lifecycle — from experiment to production.\",\"Flow:\",\"Train → Evaluate → Register → Approve → Deploy\",\"Version\",\"Track model, dataset, and code commit together.\",\"Metrics\",\"Store evaluation scores, hyperparameters, and owner info.\",\"Governance\",\"Approval workflows, deployment status, and rollback capability.\"],\"color\":\"from-amber-500/20 to-orange-500/10 border-amber-500/30\"},{\"slideNum\":8,\"tag\":\"Slide 8\",\"heading\":\"CI/CD for Machine Learning\",\"subheading\":\"ML pipelines extend traditional CI/CD by adding data validation, model training, and performance gates before any deployment proceeds.\",\"bullets\":[\"Unit Tests\",\"Code and data tests must pass\",\"Performance Eval\",\"Compute accuracy, F1, AUC\",\"Data Validation\",\"Check schema, quality, and drift\",\"Quality Gate\",\"Metrics must meet thresholds\",\"Model Training\",\"Retrain on validated data\",\"Quality Gate Examples\",\"Accuracy ≥ 90%\",\"F1 ≥ 85%\",\"AUC ≥ 90%\",\"Key Difference from Traditional CI/CD\",\"Standard pipelines test code only. ML CI/CD must also validate\",\"data quality\",\"and\",\"model performance\",\"— a failing metric blocks deployment automatically.\"],\"color\":\"from-blue-500/20 to-indigo-500/10 border-blue-500/30\"},{\"slideNum\":9,\"tag\":\"Slide 9\",\"heading\":\"Docker for ML\",\"subheading\":\"Solving &quot;It Works on My Machine&quot;\",\"bullets\":[\"Docker packages your application, Python runtime, PyTorch, dependencies, and model artifacts into a single portable\",\"container\",\"— eliminating environment drift between development and production.\",\"Images are stored in\",\"Docker Hub\",\"Amazon ECR\",\", or a private registry.\",\"01\",\"Write Dockerfile\",\"Define base image, dependencies, and entry point.\",\"02\",\"Build Docker Image\",\"Creates a reproducible snapshot of the environment.\",\"03\",\"Run Container\",\"Deploy consistently across any host or cloud.\"],\"color\":\"from-emerald-500/20 to-teal-500/10 border-emerald-500/30\"},{\"slideNum\":10,\"tag\":\"Slide 10\",\"heading\":\"End-to-End Deep Learning Lifecycle\",\"subheading\":\"Production AI is not a single model — it is an\",\"bullets\":[\"automated, governed lifecycle\",\"connecting every stage from raw data to continuous improvement.\",\"01\",\"Data\",\"Collect, clean, and version datasets.\",\"02\",\"Deep Learning & PyTorch\",\"Design and train neural network models.\",\"03\",\"Transformers\",\"Apply self-attention architectures for NLP, vision, and multimodal tasks.\",\"04\",\"Distributed Training\",\"Scale across multiple GPUs for large models.\",\"05\",\"Model Evaluation\",\"Measure accuracy, F1, AUC, and other metrics.\",\"06\",\"Model Registry\",\"Version, track, and govern model artifacts.\",\"07\",\"CI/CD\",\"Automate testing, quality gates, and deployment pipelines.\",\"08\",\"Docker\",\"Package models into reproducible containers.\",\"09\",\"Deployment\",\"Serve models to production environments.\",\"10\",\"Monitoring & Continuous Improvement\",\"Track drift, retrain, and iterate.\",\"Takeaway:\",\"Every tool in this stack serves a purpose — together they form a reliable, scalable path from experiment to production AI.\"],\"color\":\"from-purple-500/20 to-pink-500/10 border-purple-500/30\"}]",
